{"id":"expl:packages/core/src/source-policy.ts@L25","kind":"explanation","commentRef":{"file":"packages/core/src/source-policy.ts","span":{"start":25,"end":28}},"file":"packages/core/src/source-policy.ts","span":{"start":25,"end":28},"lang":"typescript","hash":"blake3:f2ef01f6649d40deb173d6e1d6428fd2b246b9a041767e64905143b627e3ae77","meta":{"text":"Resolve a node's source policy. An explicit `meta.sourcePolicy` wins; absent that, a node whose\nAST type is `property` (or flagged `meta.valueRedacted`) defaults to `redact-properties`."}}
{"id":"expl:packages/core/src/source-policy.ts@L47","kind":"explanation","commentRef":{"file":"packages/core/src/source-policy.ts","span":{"start":47,"end":52}},"file":"packages/core/src/source-policy.ts","span":{"start":47,"end":52},"lang":"typescript","hash":"blake3:d667099a464a523a4f0b13c6a2e26cef0d37a9e2d84d2d3b16205917d76e9fd5","meta":{"text":"Redact a `.properties` text block: keep keys (and structural position) but drop every value to\n`<redacted>`. Comments (`#`/`!`) and blank lines are dropped entirely — they carry no searchable\nstructure and would only bloat the FTS body. A line without a `:`/`=` separator is treated as a\nkey with an empty value (`key=<redacted>`)."}}
{"id":"expl:packages/core/src/source-policy.ts@L66","kind":"explanation","commentRef":{"file":"packages/core/src/source-policy.ts","span":{"start":66,"end":71}},"file":"packages/core/src/source-policy.ts","span":{"start":66,"end":71},"lang":"typescript","hash":"blake3:17e4775663d7c57101c29e8da2556631f0c28297ee44d7803901a244e60034c6","meta":{"text":"Redact secret attribute values in Mule XML config text while keeping placeholder references. An\nattribute whose name matches `password|secret|token|credential|private-key` (case-insensitive) is\nreplaced by its placeholder when the value is a `${...}` or `secure::...` reference (so the\nproperty key remains searchable), otherwise `<redacted>`. Non-secret attributes pass through."}}
